From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:50:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] drm/msm: make the GPU devfreq up-threshold a parameter

msm.gpu_devfreq_upthreshold (percent busy, default 50 = the value so far)
sets the simple_ondemand up-threshold of the GPU, for an A/B of frame pacing
against power without a rebuild.

Measurements behind the idea: Reixo0 on SM8850, in github Reixo0/linux
commit 81aeecda5b6c ("drm/msm: throttle the GPU up at 20% load")
(20 % for 144 Hz scrolling at ~0.1 W more on video, later back to 50 %;
no Signed-off-by).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu_devfreq.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu_devfreq.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu_devfreq.c
index f3c664b20a1ba..90f5a1f708ad0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu_devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu_devfreq.c
@@ -12,6 +12,14 @@
 #include <linux/math64.h>
 #include <linux/units.h>
 
+/*
+ * iceland switch: the simple_ondemand up-threshold of the GPU, percent busy (default 50 = before). Reixo0 measured
+ * 20 for smoother 144 Hz scrolling at about 0.1 W more on video on SM8850 (81aeecda5b6c, then back to 50).
+ */
+static unsigned int gpu_devfreq_upthreshold = 50;
+module_param(gpu_devfreq_upthreshold, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(gpu_devfreq_upthreshold, "iceland: GPU devfreq up-threshold, % busy, 11..100 (default 50)");
+
 /*
  * Power Management:
  */
@@ -152,7 +160,7 @@ void msm_devfreq_init(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 	 * where due to stalling waiting for vblank we could get stuck
 	 * at (for ex) 30fps at 50% utilization.
 	 */
-	priv->gpu_devfreq_config.upthreshold = 50;
+	priv->gpu_devfreq_config.upthreshold = clamp(gpu_devfreq_upthreshold, 11U, 100U);
 	priv->gpu_devfreq_config.downdifferential = 10;
 
 	mutex_init(&df->lock);
-- 
